Package: ventro
Title: Let Command Line Tools Speak in R Help Pages
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: person("Athanasia M.", "Mowinckel", , "a.m.mowinckel@psykologi.uio.no",
    role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-5756-0223"))
Description: Embeds the help output of a command line tool into R help
    pages at render time, so help reflects the tool installed on the
    user's machine when the page is viewed. Output is escaped for Rd,
    cleaned of terminal formatting, and replaced by a short notice when
    the tool is missing, so rendering never fails. Use it from 'roxygen2'
    inline 'Rd' code, or through the optional '@clihelp' tag.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Depends: R (>= 4.0.1)
Encoding: UTF-8
Imports:
    processx (>= 3.5.0)
Suggests: 
    knitr,
    rmarkdown,
    roxygen2 (>= 7.2.0),
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    withr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.1
VignetteBuilder: knitr
